+# AI log — SCRUM-80 (US5 · F-37 SMAC inactivity) — 2026-10-20
+
+**Author:** Yeison Delgado · **Tool:** Claude (Claude Code)
+
+## What the AI generated
+- `backend/src/nodes/smac-state.ts`: default threshold (3 h) and `SMAC_INACTIVITY_SQL`.
+- Changes in `backend/src/nodes/nodes.service.ts`: `smac_inactive` in each node, `smacInactivityFor()`,
+  and one shared reader for the Falcon and SMAC thresholds.
+- Unit tests in `nodes.service.spec.ts` and the e2e test `backend/test/smac-inactivity.e2e-spec.ts`.
+
+## What I did / reviewed
+- Followed Sofia's notes and the Falcon implementation (US6) so both work the same way.
+- Checked the rule against the spec: RF-ING-01 (3 h, configurable) and annex §4.1 (the three SMAC tables are not aligned,
+  so the newest record of the three is used).
+- Ran: unit tests (68 pass), lint, build, and the e2e test on a local PostgreSQL with
+  `01/02/03` SQL files (7 pass). With `SMAC_INACTIVITY_HOURS=5` the 4 h cases fail as expected.
+
+## Review of F-36 (SCRUM-79)
+Already covered by US6 (`FUSE_SUMMARY_SQL`): a Falcon with no record, or older than `FALCON_INACTIVITY_HOURS`, makes the node gray.
